SELECT latn FROM (SELECT round(LAT_N, 4) as latn,
    ROW_NUMBER() over(order by LAT_N asc) as rn,
    COUNT(*) over() as total
FROM STATION) s where s.rn = (s.total+1)/2;


ROW_NUMBER():
assigns a unique sequential number to each row.

OVER():
tells the SQL which rows the window function should operate on and in what order.

ROUND():
rounds a number to a specified number of decimal places.
